        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c065088c-0d1c-541a-9806-c8dc09900af1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rufus Wainwright\n- Products: Release the Stars, Going to a Town, Vibrate: The Best of Rufus Wainwright, Waiting for a Want\n- Companies: DreamWorks Records\n- Topics: singles, studio releases, greatest hits albums, EP releases\n\nFacts:\n- Rufus Wainwright's self-titled debut album was released in 1998.\n- Rufus Wainwright's album Poses was released in 2001.\n- Rufus Wainwright's album Want One was released in 2003.\n- Waiting for a Want is the first EP by Rufus Wainwright, and DreamWorks Records released it electronically on June 29, 2004.\n- Rufus Wainwright's album Want Two was released in 2004.\n- Rufus Wainwright's album Release the Stars was released in 2007.\n- Release the Stars generated the singles Going to a Town, Rules and Regulations, and Tiergarten.\n- Going to a Town is a song written and performed by Canadian-American singer-songwriter Rufus Wainwright.\n- Going to a Town peaked at number 54 on the UK Singles Chart.\n- Rufus Wainwright's album Out of the Game was released in 2012.\n- The standard edition of Vibrate: The Best of Rufus Wainwright includes eighteen songs from six of Rufus Wainwright's studio releases, plus soundtrack contributions and the previously unreleased track Me and Liza.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "17fe5587-a9b6-51e4-9d7c-bb8e92954e54",
        "text": "Page: Release the Stars. Sentence: The album generated three singles: \"Going to a Town\", which peaked at number 54 on the UK Singles Chart, \"Rules and Regulations\", and \"Tiergarten\".\nPage: Going to a Town. Sentence: \"Going to a Town\" is a song written and performed by Canadian-American singer-songwriter Rufus Wainwright.\nPage: Vibrate: The Best of Rufus Wainwright. Sentence: The standard issue of the album includes eighteen songs from six of Wainwright's studio releases, including his self-titled debut album (1998), \"Poses\" (2001), \"Want One\" (2003), \"Want Two\" (2004), \"Release the Stars\" (2007) and \"Out of the Game\" (2012), plus soundtrack contributions and one previously unreleased track (\"Me and Liza\").\nPage: Waiting for a Want. Sentence: Waiting for a Want is the first EP by Canadian-American singer-songwriter Rufus Wainwright, released through DreamWorks Records electronically on June 29, 2004.",
